+def _split_provenance_note(d: Path) -> str:
+    """One sentence of split-child provenance context, or "" — shared by the plan and
+    split prompts (issue #458).
+
+    Both prompts already tell the model to split an oversized brief; neither said the one
+    thing that keeps a split child from being told to re-split itself over evidence it
+    inherited from the split that produced it — a `Conflicts with:` entry naming a SPLIT
+    SIBLING, not organic new scope. `plan_policy.size_reasons` now makes that distinction
+    for the DRIVER's own advisory (keyed on the sibling id actually being declared, never
+    on the lineage record's mere presence — a bundle with organic-only conflicts is still
+    told to split). The model reads the same brief before that advisory runs again, so the
+    same context has to travel with the prompt or a session routinely re-proposes the
+    split the advisory would tell it not to.
+    """
